 s9329053@sandcastle.cosc.brocku.ca (Darcy Boese) writes...
> I got everything compiled all right (I think) and when I run the script
> "nethack" I get the error message:
>       Can't find file perm to lock!
> Any ideas what I need to do to fix this?

     You need to do `make install' in the "top" directory (the one above
"src", "include", and so on) to setup the playground directory properly.
If you were to create "perm" manually, your next discovery would likely
be that you couldn't save games because the "save" subdirectory wasn't
available.

     Do not try to make the playground be a directory which already has
anything in it (such as "top" itself!), because one of the things `make
install' does is clear out the contents of the destination directory and
any subdirectories it may have.  Also, you need to update the top Makefile
to specify GAMEDIR to be the same location as was compiled into the game
as HACKDIR, and to specify ownership of the playground directory (GAMEUID
and GAMEGRP).



